# Network phase N5: `tftp get` / `tftp put`, against a TFTP server run by the test.
@net
@tftp
$ net dhcp
~ ^address 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP\)
$ tftp get {tftp} hello.txt
received 27 bytes into /hello.txt
$ cat hello.txt
Hello from the TFTP server
# A file made here goes to the server and comes back unchanged.
$ echo written inside BeeCodersOs > note.txt
$ tftp put {tftp} note.txt
sent 27 bytes as note.txt
$ tftp get {tftp} note.txt back.txt
received 27 bytes into /back.txt
$ cat back.txt
written inside BeeCodersOs
# 200 000 bytes of binary data, there and back: 391 blocks each way.
$ tftp get {tftp} big.bin
~ ^received 200000 bytes into /big\.bin
$ tftp put {tftp} big.bin copy.bin
~ ^sent 200000 bytes as copy\.bin
$ tftp get {tftp} compare:big.bin:copy.bin verdict
$ cat verdict
big.bin and copy.bin are identical (200000 bytes)
# Sizes around one block, and an empty file.
$ tftp get {tftp} empty
received 0 bytes into /empty
$ tftp put {tftp} empty empty2
sent 0 bytes as empty2
$ tftp get {tftp} compare:empty:empty2 verdict
$ cat verdict
empty and empty2 are identical (0 bytes)
# Into a directory, under the same name.
$ mkdir inbox
$ tftp get {tftp} hello.txt inbox
received 27 bytes into /inbox/hello.txt
# Errors from the server and from here.
$ tftp get {tftp} missing.txt
missing.txt: the server says: file not found
$ ls
!~ missing
$ tftp put {tftp} note.txt readonly
readonly: the server says: access denied
$ tftp put {tftp} nothere.txt
~ ^nothere\.txt: 
$ tftp
~ ^usage: tftp get HOST\[:PORT\] FILE
